IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `caa-arbitration`

-- Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) -- the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters (the
-- Q&A layer).
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every question takes `my role`
-- first ("Which of these describes you"); a question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without
-- reading any other input. The rules are the baseline's (caa-arbitration.l4): this layer builds the baseline's records
-- from plain answers and calls its functions. The arbitrator's own duties the baseline does not ask (ss 12(1), (2), 18,
-- 24(4), (5), 30(1), 33(2)) are added here as helpers, and the duties the baseline already encodes from the party's side
-- (ss 24(2), 27D, 31(3)) are asked of the arbitrator by calling the same rules, so the two seats cannot disagree.
--
-- ROLES. A party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration (the baseline's seat), and the arbitrator, or the person
-- approached to be one. The arbitrator is a private person the parties choose, and the Act puts duties on them by name
-- (s 12(1), (2), s 18, s 24, s 30, s 31, s 33), so they are a seat; the Court is never one.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act layer). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise
-- for you` without reading anything else. For the party: a court case brought about a dispute the agreement covers
-- (s 8); an arbitrator appointed (ss 12, 18, 24, 27D(1)); the arbitrator having mediated, the mediation ended (s 27D(4)-
-- (6), shared with the arbitrator); a settlement (s 30); and the award (`The award and me`: no award yet gives `does
-- not arise for you` for every award question; an award wholly in my favour for the resisting question; an award wholly
-- against me for the enforcing question). For the arbitrator: the parties having settled during the proceedings
-- (s 30(1)); a party having asked for a correction (s 33(2)); and the mediation, as for the party. The questions about
-- the agreement, the Act's reach and the appointment arise for every party and take none.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration`
    `I am an arbitrator, or have been asked to be one`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

-- The s 33(2) answer: the days to make a justified correction, or that it need not be made.
DECLARE `Correction time` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `you need not make it, as you do not consider the request justified`
    `within` HAS `number of days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Arbitrators` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `arbitrators` HAS `number of arbitrators` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Reach answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the Act's reach` HAS `how much applies` IS A `How much of the Act applies`

DECLARE `Appointment answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `appointed by` HAS `who appoints` IS A `Who appoints`

DECLARE `Settlement answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the settlement binds` HAS `how it binds` IS A `How my settlement binds`

DECLARE `Mediation answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `after the mediation` HAS `what follows` IS AN `After the mediation`

DECLARE `Setting aside answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `setting aside` HAS `the outcome of the application` IS A `Setting aside`

DECLARE `Appeal answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the appeal` HAS `the outcome of the appeal` IS AN `Appeal`

DECLARE `What I must do on a settlement` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `terminate the proceedings, and record the settlement as an award on agreed terms`
    `terminate the proceedings; you need not record the settlement as an award`

-- The party's award situation. Every award question does not arise before an award; the enforcing question does not
-- arise for an award wholly against me, nor the resisting question for one wholly in my favour.
DECLARE `The award and me` IS ONE OF
    `no award has been made yet`
    `an award has been made, in my favour`
    `an award has been made, against me`
    `an award has been made, partly in my favour and partly against me`

§§ `Building the baseline's inputs, and the situations`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `recorded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `electronic` IS A BOOLEAN
      `pleaded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `commercial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Model Law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `seated in WA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My arbitration agreement`
`the agreement built from` MEANS
    `My arbitration agreement` WITH
        `we agreed to arbitrate disputes about a defined legal relationship` IS `agreed`
        `its content is recorded in some form` IS `recorded`
        `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference` IS `electronic`
        `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence` IS `pleaded`
        `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause it makes part of the contract` IS `incorporated`
        `both parties had their places of business in Australia when it was made` IS `in Australia`
        `the relationship is commercial` IS `commercial`
        `the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974` IS `Model Law`
        `the place of arbitration is in Western Australia` IS `seated in WA`

GIVEN `procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `failure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `other means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `arbitrators` IS A NUMBER
      `parties` IS A NUMBER
      `agree sole` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days to appoint` IS A NUMBER
      `days to third` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `My appointment facts`
`the appointment built from` MEANS
    `My appointment facts` WITH
        `we agreed an appointment procedure` IS `procedure`
        `under it a party failed to act, agreement failed, or an institution failed to act` IS `failure`
        `the procedure provides other means of securing the appointment` IS `other means`
        `the number of arbitrators` IS `arbitrators`
        `the number of parties` IS `parties`
        `we agree on the sole arbitrator` IS `agree sole`
        `days since the other party received my request to appoint, still not appointing` IS `days to appoint`
        `days since the two party arbitrators were appointed, still no third` IS `days to third`

GIVEN `equal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `opportunity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `asked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no hearings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `passed on` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reports` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How I was heard`
`the hearing built from` MEANS
    `How I was heard` WITH
        `I was treated equally with the other party` IS `equal`
        `I had a reasonable opportunity to present my case` IS `opportunity`
        `I asked for an oral hearing` IS `asked`
        `we agreed that no hearings would be held` IS `no hearings`
        `an oral hearing was held` IS `held`
        `I had sufficient advance notice of every hearing and inspection` IS `notice`
        `everything the other party gave the tribunal was communicated to me` IS `passed on`
        `every expert report or document the tribunal may rely on was communicated to me` IS `reports`

GIVEN `capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `beyond` IS A BOOLEAN
      `separable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `departed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not arbitrable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `public policy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `received` IS A DATE
      `s 33 request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `disposed` IS A DATE
      `applied` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `My setting-aside application`
`the application built from` MEANS
    `My setting-aside application` WITH
        `I prove a party lacked capacity or the agreement is invalid` IS `capacity`
        `I prove I had no proper notice or could not present my case` IS `no notice`
        `I prove the award goes beyond the submission to arbitration` IS `beyond`
        `the part beyond the submission can be separated` IS `separable`
        `I prove the tribunal or procedure departed from our agreement or the Act` IS `departed`
        `the Court finds the dispute not capable of settlement by arbitration` IS `not arbitrable`
        `the Court finds the award against the public policy of Western Australia` IS `public policy`
        `the date I received the award` IS `received`
        `a section 33 request was made` IS `s 33 request`
        `the date the tribunal disposed of it` IS `disposed`
        `the date I apply` IS `applied`

GIVEN `question of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `agreed to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `affects rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `asked to decide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `obviously wrong` IS A BOOLEAN
      `public importance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `just and proper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `received` IS A DATE
      `s 33 request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `disposed` IS A DATE
      `appealed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `My appeal`
`the appeal built from` MEANS
    `My appeal` WITH
        `it is a question of law arising out of the award` IS `question of law`
        `the parties agreed to an appeal before the appeal period ended` IS `agreed to appeal`
        `the Court is satisfied it will substantially affect a party's rights` IS `affects rights`
        `the Court is satisfied the tribunal was asked to decide it` IS `asked to decide`
        `the Court is satisfied the decision is obviously wrong` IS `obviously wrong`
        `the Court is satisfied it is of general public importance and the decision open to serious doubt` IS `public importance`
        `the Court is satisfied it is just and proper for the Court to decide it` IS `just and proper`
        `the date I received the award` IS `received`
        `a section 33 request was made` IS `s 33 request`
        `the date the tribunal disposed of it` IS `disposed`
        `the date I appeal` IS `appealed`

-- The award situations list every value, with no OTHERWISE: a CONSIDER with OTHERWISE takes it for an ASSUMEd value
-- instead of failing (graffiti finding 31), so the "not read" cases would prove nothing.
GIVEN `the award and me` IS A `The award and me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no award has been made` IF
    CONSIDER `the award and me`
    WHEN `no award has been made yet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an award has been made, in my favour` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an award has been made, against me` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an award has been made, partly in my favour and partly against me` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the award and me` IS A `The award and me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is no award in my favour to enforce` IF
    CONSIDER `the award and me`
    WHEN `no award has been made yet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an award has been made, in my favour` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an award has been made, against me` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an award has been made, partly in my favour and partly against me` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `the award and me` IS A `The award and me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is no award against me to resist` IF
    CONSIDER `the award and me`
    WHEN `no award has been made yet` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an award has been made, in my favour` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an award has been made, against me` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an award has been made, partly in my favour and partly against me` THEN FALSE

-- s 12(1): "When a person is approached in connection with the person's possible appointment as an arbitrator, the person
-- must disclose any circumstances likely to give rise to justifiable doubts as to the person's impartiality or
-- independence." (2): "An arbitrator, from the time of the arbitrator's appointment and throughout the arbitral
-- proceedings, must without delay disclose any circumstances of the kind referred to in subsection (1) to the parties
-- unless they have already been informed of them by the arbitrator." (5): "justifiable doubts ... only if there is a real
-- danger of bias". So once appointed, there is nothing more to disclose of a circumstance the arbitrator has already told
-- the parties of.
GIVEN `there are circumstances likely to show a real danger of bias` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have already told the parties of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12(1), (2) -- the arbitrator must disclose the circumstances` IF
        `there are circumstances likely to show a real danger of bias`
    AND (    (NOT `I have been appointed`)
          OR (NOT `I have already told the parties of them`))

-- s 30(1): "If, during arbitral proceedings, the parties settle the dispute, the arbitral tribunal must terminate the
-- proceedings and, if requested by the parties and not objected to by the arbitral tribunal, record the settlement in the
-- form of an arbitral award on agreed terms."
GIVEN `the parties asked me to record it as an award` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I object to recording it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What I must do on a settlement`
`s 30(1) -- what the tribunal must do on a settlement` MEANS
    IF `the parties asked me to record it as an award` AND (NOT `I object to recording it`)
    THEN `terminate the proceedings, and record the settlement as an award on agreed terms`
    ELSE `terminate the proceedings; you need not record the settlement as an award`

-- s 33(2): "If the arbitral tribunal considers a request under subsection (1) to be justified, it must make the correction
-- or give the interpretation within 30 days of receipt of the request."
`s 33(2) -- the days the tribunal has to correct the award` MEANS 30

§§ `For a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration`

§§§ `ss 1, 7 -- is my arbitration agreement binding, and does the Act apply`

-- Each question takes only the agreement's facts its baseline rule reads; the rest get fixed placeholders it never
-- reads (the rules' ANDs and ORs stop before them).
@export Is my arbitration agreement in writing (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 7(3)-(8))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `its content is recorded in some form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the content of your agreement to arbitrate is recorded in any form, even if the agreement was made orally or by conduct
      `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is in an electronic communication (such as an email) whose information is accessible for later reference
      `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one party alleged the agreement in a statement of claim and the other did not deny it in the defence
      `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause becomes part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract refers to a document (such as standard terms) containing an arbitration clause, so as to make that clause part of the contract
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is our arbitration agreement in writing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN `yes if` (`Is my arbitration agreement in writing` (`the agreement built from` TRUE `its content is recorded in some form` `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference` `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence` `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause becomes part of it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I have an arbitration agreement the Act recognises (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 7)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `we agreed to arbitrate disputes about a defined legal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other party agreed to submit to arbitration all or some disputes that have arisen or may arise between you about a defined legal relationship, contractual or not
      `its content is recorded in some form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the content of your agreement to arbitrate is recorded in any form, even if the agreement was made orally or by conduct
      `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is in an electronic communication (such as an email) whose information is accessible for later reference
      `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one party alleged the agreement in a statement of claim and the other did not deny it in the defence
      `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause becomes part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract refers to a document (such as standard terms) containing an arbitration clause, so as to make that clause part of the contract
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do we have an arbitration agreement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN `yes if` (`Do I have an arbitration agreement` (`the agreement built from` `we agreed to arbitrate disputes about a defined legal relationship` `its content is recorded in some form` `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference` `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence` `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause becomes part of it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my arbitration a domestic commercial arbitration under the Act (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 1(1), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `we agreed to arbitrate disputes about a defined legal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other party agreed to submit to arbitration all or some disputes that have arisen or may arise between you about a defined legal relationship, contractual or not
      `its content is recorded in some form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the content of your agreement to arbitrate is recorded in any form, even if the agreement was made orally or by conduct
      `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is in an electronic communication (such as an email) whose information is accessible for later reference
      `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one party alleged the agreement in a statement of claim and the other did not deny it in the defence
      `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause becomes part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract refers to a document (such as standard terms) containing an arbitration clause, so as to make that clause part of the contract
      `both parties had their places of business in Australia when it was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the agreement was made, both parties had their places of business in Australia
      `the relationship is commercial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relationship the dispute is about is commercial (read widely)
      `the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arbitration is one to which the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974 (Cth)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is ours a domestic commercial arbitration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN `yes if` (`Is my arbitration a domestic commercial arbitration` (`the agreement built from` `we agreed to arbitrate disputes about a defined legal relationship` `its content is recorded in some form` `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference` `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence` `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause becomes part of it` `both parties had their places of business in Australia when it was made` `the relationship is commercial` `the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974` FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much of the Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) applies to my arbitration (s 1)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `we agreed to arbitrate disputes about a defined legal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other party agreed to submit to arbitration all or some disputes that have arisen or may arise between you about a defined legal relationship, contractual or not
      `its content is recorded in some form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the content of your agreement to arbitrate is recorded in any form, even if the agreement was made orally or by conduct
      `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is in an electronic communication (such as an email) whose information is accessible for later reference
      `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one party alleged the agreement in a statement of claim and the other did not deny it in the defence
      `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause becomes part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract refers to a document (such as standard terms) containing an arbitration clause, so as to make that clause part of the contract
      `both parties had their places of business in Australia when it was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the agreement was made, both parties had their places of business in Australia
      `the relationship is commercial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relationship the dispute is about is commercial (read widely)
      `the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arbitration is one to which the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974 (Cth)
      `the place of arbitration is in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place (seat) of the arbitration is in Western Australia
GIVETH A `Reach answer`
`How much of the Act applies to our arbitration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN `the Act's reach` (`How much of the Act applies to my arbitration` (`the agreement built from` `we agreed to arbitrate disputes about a defined legal relationship` `its content is recorded in some form` `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference` `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence` `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause becomes part of it` `both parties had their places of business in Australia when it was made` `the relationship is commercial` `the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974` `the place of arbitration is in Western Australia`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 8 -- the court case (situation: a court case brought)`

-- The situation is the baseline's "the court action is in a matter the agreement covers", so within it that input is
-- TRUE. The place of arbitration is not read by s 8 (s 1(2) applies s 8 wherever the seat is); it gets a placeholder.
@export Must the court refer my dispute to arbitration (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 8(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a court case has been brought about a dispute my arbitration agreement covers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court case has been brought in a matter your arbitration agreement covers
      `we agreed to arbitrate disputes about a defined legal relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other party agreed to submit to arbitration all or some disputes that have arisen or may arise between you about a defined legal relationship, contractual or not
      `its content is recorded in some form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the content of your agreement to arbitrate is recorded in any form, even if the agreement was made orally or by conduct
      `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is in an electronic communication (such as an email) whose information is accessible for later reference
      `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one party alleged the agreement in a statement of claim and the other did not deny it in the defence
      `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause becomes part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract refers to a document (such as standard terms) containing an arbitration clause, so as to make that clause part of the contract
      `both parties had their places of business in Australia when it was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the agreement was made, both parties had their places of business in Australia
      `the relationship is commercial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relationship the dispute is about is commercial (read widely)
      `the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arbitration is one to which the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974 (Cth)
      `a party asked for referral no later than its first statement on the substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a party asked the court to refer the dispute to arbitration no later than its first statement on the substance of the dispute
      `the court finds the agreement null and void, inoperative or incapable of being performed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The court's finding about the agreement (asked, not guessed)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the court send our dispute to arbitration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF NOT `a court case has been brought about a dispute my arbitration agreement covers` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must the court refer my dispute to arbitration` (`the agreement built from` `we agreed to arbitrate disputes about a defined legal relationship` `its content is recorded in some form` `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference` `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence` `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause becomes part of it` `both parties had their places of business in Australia when it was made` `the relationship is commercial` `the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974` FALSE) TRUE `a party asked for referral no later than its first statement on the substance` `the court finds the agreement null and void, inoperative or incapable of being performed`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 10, 11 -- the arbitrators, and who appoints them`

@export How many arbitrators will hear my dispute (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 10)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the number of arbitrators we agreed` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of arbitrators you and the other party agreed (0 if you did not agree one)
GIVETH AN `Arbitrators`
`How many arbitrators will hear our dispute` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN arbitrators (`How many arbitrators will there be` `the number of arbitrators we agreed`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Who appoints the arbitrator in my arbitration (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `we agreed an appointment procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties agreed a procedure for appointing the arbitrator or arbitrators
      `under it a party, the parties or an institution failed to act or agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under that procedure, whether a party failed to act, the parties or arbitrators could not agree, or an institution failed to perform its function
      `the procedure provides other means of securing the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreed procedure provides other means of securing the appointment
      `the number of arbitrators` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of arbitrators (one unless the parties agreed otherwise)
      `the number of parties` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of parties to the arbitration
      `we agree on the sole arbitrator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc With a sole arbitrator, whether the parties agree on who it is
      `days since the other party got my request to appoint, still not appointing` IS A NUMBER @desc With three arbitrators and two parties, the days since the other party received your request to appoint its arbitrator, if it still has not
      `days since the two party arbitrators were appointed, still no third` IS A NUMBER @desc With three arbitrators and two parties, the days since the two party-appointed arbitrators were appointed, if they have not agreed on the third
GIVETH AN `Appointment answer`
`Who appoints our arbitrator` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN `appointed by` (`Who appoints the arbitrator` (`the appointment built from` `we agreed an appointment procedure` `under it a party, the parties or an institution failed to act or agree` `the procedure provides other means of securing the appointment` `the number of arbitrators` `the number of parties` `we agree on the sole arbitrator` `days since the other party got my request to appoint, still not appointing` `days since the two party arbitrators were appointed, still no third`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 12, 18, 24, 27D(1) -- the arbitrator and my hearing (situation: an arbitrator appointed)`

@export May I challenge the arbitrator (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 12(3), (4), (6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an arbitrator has been appointed in my arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an arbitrator has been appointed in your arbitration
      `there is a real danger of bias on the arbitrator's part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a real danger of bias (as the tribunal or Court would find)
      `the arbitrator lacks a qualification we agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arbitrator lacks a qualification the parties agreed on
      `I appointed or took part in appointing the arbitrator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you appointed the arbitrator or took part in the appointment
      `I learned the reason only after the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became aware of the reason only after the appointment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I challenge our arbitrator` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF NOT `an arbitrator has been appointed in my arbitration` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I challenge the arbitrator` `there is a real danger of bias on the arbitrator's part` `the arbitrator lacks a qualification we agreed` `I appointed or took part in appointing the arbitrator` `I learned the reason only after the appointment`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the tribunal hold an oral hearing if I ask for one (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 24(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an arbitrator has been appointed in my arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an arbitrator has been appointed in your arbitration
      `I asked for an oral hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked the tribunal for an oral hearing
      `we agreed that no hearings would be held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties agreed there would be no hearings
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the tribunal give me an oral hearing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF NOT `an arbitrator has been appointed in my arbitration` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must the tribunal hold an oral hearing` `I asked for an oral hearing` `we agreed that no hearings would be held`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have I been denied the hearing the Act gives me (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) ss 18, 24)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an arbitrator has been appointed in my arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an arbitrator has been appointed in your arbitration
      `I was treated equally with the other party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the tribunal treated you equally with the other party
      `I had a reasonable opportunity to present my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a reasonable opportunity to present your case
      `I asked for an oral hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked the tribunal for an oral hearing
      `we agreed that no hearings would be held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties agreed there would be no hearings
      `an oral hearing was held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an oral hearing was held
      `I had sufficient advance notice of every hearing and inspection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had sufficient advance notice of every hearing, and of every meeting to inspect goods, property or documents
      `everything the other party gave the tribunal was passed on to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every statement, document or other information the other party supplied to the tribunal was communicated to you
      `every expert report or document the tribunal may rely on was passed on to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every expert report or evidentiary document the tribunal may rely on was communicated to you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I been denied my hearing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF NOT `an arbitrator has been appointed in my arbitration` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Have I been denied my right to be heard` (`the hearing built from` `I was treated equally with the other party` `I had a reasonable opportunity to present my case` `I asked for an oral hearing` `we agreed that no hearings would be held` `an oral hearing was held` `I had sufficient advance notice of every hearing and inspection` `everything the other party gave the tribunal was passed on to me` `every expert report or document the tribunal may rely on was passed on to me`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May our arbitrator act as mediator in our dispute (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 27D(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an arbitrator has been appointed in my arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an arbitrator has been appointed in your arbitration
      `our arbitration agreement provides for the arbitrator to mediate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arbitration agreement provides for the arbitrator to act as mediator
      `each party has consented in writing to the arbitrator mediating` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every party has consented in writing to the arbitrator acting as mediator
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May our arbitrator mediate our dispute` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF NOT `an arbitrator has been appointed in my arbitration` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May our arbitrator act as mediator` `our arbitration agreement provides for the arbitrator to mediate` `each party has consented in writing to the arbitrator mediating`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 27D(4)-(6), 30 -- mediation and settlement (situations: the arbitrator mediated; a settlement)`

-- Shared with the arbitrator's question: the same rule, the same situation input.
@export May the arbitrator who mediated our dispute now arbitrate it (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 27D(4)-(6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the arbitrator has acted as mediator, and the mediation has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arbitrator (you, or your arbitrator) has acted as mediator in the dispute, and the mediation proceedings have been terminated
      `every party consented in writing on or after the mediation ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every party gave written consent, on or after the mediation ended, to the arbitrator arbitrating
GIVETH A `Mediation answer`
`May the arbitrator who mediated go on to arbitrate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF NOT `the arbitrator has acted as mediator, and the mediation has ended` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `after the mediation` (`May the arbitrator who mediated now arbitrate` `every party consented in writing on or after the mediation ended`)
    WHEN `I am an arbitrator, or have been asked to be one` THEN
        IF NOT `the arbitrator has acted as mediator, and the mediation has ended` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `after the mediation` (`May the arbitrator who mediated now arbitrate` `every party consented in writing on or after the mediation ended`)

@export How is my settlement enforced (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 30, s 35)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `we have settled our dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other party have settled the dispute, during an arbitration or outside one (by mediation, negotiation or deed)
      `we settled during arbitral proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dispute was settled while an arbitration was under way
      `the parties asked the tribunal to record it as an award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties asked the tribunal to record the settlement as an award on agreed terms
      `the tribunal objected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the tribunal objected to recording it
GIVETH A `Settlement answer`
`How is our settlement enforced` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF NOT `we have settled our dispute` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the settlement binds` (`How is my settlement enforced` `we settled during arbitral proceedings` `the parties asked the tribunal to record it as an award` `the tribunal objected`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 31, 33, 34, 34A, 35, 36 -- the award (situation: the award and me)`

@export Must my award state its reasons (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 31(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the award and me` IS A `The award and me` @desc Whether an award has been made in your arbitration and, if so, whether it is in your favour, against you, or partly each
      `we agreed no reasons would be given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties agreed that no reasons are to be given
      `it is an award on agreed terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the award records a settlement under s 30
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must our award state its reasons` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF `no award has been made` `the award and me` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must my award state its reasons` `we agreed no reasons would be given` `it is an award on agreed terms`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I in time to ask the tribunal to correct my award (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 33(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the award and me` IS A `The award and me` @desc Whether an award has been made in your arbitration and, if so, whether it is in your favour, against you, or partly each
      `the date I received the award` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the award
      `the date of my request` IS A DATE @desc The day you send the request, with notice to the other party
      `another period we agreed, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc A different period the parties agreed (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I in time to have my award corrected` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF `no award has been made` `the award and me` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I in time to ask for a correction` `the date I received the award` `the date of my request` `another period we agreed, in days`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The grounds are not read for the time question; they get fixed placeholders.
@export Am I in time to apply to set aside my award (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 34(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the award and me` IS A `The award and me` @desc Whether an award has been made in your arbitration and, if so, whether it is in your favour, against you, or partly each
      `the date I received the award` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the award
      `a section 33 request was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a party asked the tribunal under s 33 to correct or interpret the award, or to make an additional award
      `the date the tribunal disposed of the s 33 request` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the tribunal disposed of that request
      `the date I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply, or will apply, to the Court
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I in time to have my award set aside` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF `no award has been made` `the award and me` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I in time to apply to set aside the award` (`the application built from` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the date I received the award` `a section 33 request was made` `the date the tribunal disposed of the s 33 request` `the date I apply`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I have my award set aside, and how much of it (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 34)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the award and me` IS A `The award and me` @desc Whether an award has been made in your arbitration and, if so, whether it is in your favour, against you, or partly each
      `the date I received the award` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the award
      `a section 33 request was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a party asked the tribunal under s 33 to correct or interpret the award, or to make an additional award
      `the date the tribunal disposed of the s 33 request` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the tribunal disposed of that request
      `the date I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply, or will apply, to the Court
      `I prove a party lacked capacity or the agreement is invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can prove a party to the agreement was under some incapacity, or the agreement is not valid
      `I prove I had no proper notice or could not present my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can prove you were not given proper notice of the appointment or the proceedings, or were otherwise unable to present your case
      `I prove the award goes beyond the submission to arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can prove the award deals with a dispute, or decides matters, beyond the submission to arbitration
      `the part beyond the submission can be separated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether the decisions beyond the submission can be separated from the rest
      `I prove the tribunal or procedure departed from our agreement or the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can prove the tribunal's composition or the procedure was not as the parties agreed or, failing agreement, as the Act requires
      `the Court finds the dispute not capable of settlement by arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Court's finding that the subject matter cannot be settled by arbitration under WA law (asked, not guessed)
      `the Court finds the award against the public policy of Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Court's finding that the award conflicts with WA public policy (asked, not guessed)
GIVETH A `Setting aside answer`
`Can I have our award set aside` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF `no award has been made` `the award and me` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `setting aside` (`Can I have my award set aside` (`the application built from` `I prove a party lacked capacity or the agreement is invalid` `I prove I had no proper notice or could not present my case` `I prove the award goes beyond the submission to arbitration` `the part beyond the submission can be separated` `I prove the tribunal or procedure departed from our agreement or the Act` `the Court finds the dispute not capable of settlement by arbitration` `the Court finds the award against the public policy of Western Australia` `the date I received the award` `a section 33 request was made` `the date the tribunal disposed of the s 33 request` `the date I apply`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The leave question reads only the Court's satisfaction; the other appeal fields get fixed placeholders (the dates
-- are built with daydate's Date, imported here as the baseline's rule file imports it).
@export May the Court grant me leave to appeal (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 34A(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the award and me` IS A `The award and me` @desc Whether an award has been made in your arbitration and, if so, whether it is in your favour, against you, or partly each
      `the Court is satisfied it will substantially affect a party's rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied that deciding the question will substantially affect the rights of a party
      `the Court is satisfied the tribunal was asked to decide it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied the tribunal was asked to decide the question
      `the Court is satisfied the decision is obviously wrong` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied, on the award's findings of fact, that the tribunal's decision is obviously wrong
      `the Court is satisfied it is of general public importance and the decision open to serious doubt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied the question is of general public importance and the decision at least open to serious doubt
      `the Court is satisfied it is just and proper for the Court to decide it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied it is just and proper, despite the agreement to arbitrate, for the Court to decide the question
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Court give me leave to appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF `no award has been made` `the award and me` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May the Court grant leave to appeal` (`the appeal built from` TRUE TRUE `the Court is satisfied it will substantially affect a party's rights` `the Court is satisfied the tribunal was asked to decide it` `the Court is satisfied the decision is obviously wrong` `the Court is satisfied it is of general public importance and the decision open to serious doubt` `the Court is satisfied it is just and proper for the Court to decide it` (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 1 2000)))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I appeal against my award on a question of law (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 34A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the award and me` IS A `The award and me` @desc Whether an award has been made in your arbitration and, if so, whether it is in your favour, against you, or partly each
      `it is a question of law arising out of the award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the appeal is on a question of law arising out of the award
      `the parties agreed to an appeal before the appeal period ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties agreed, before the 3-month appeal period ended, that an appeal may be made
      `the date I received the award` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the award
      `a section 33 request was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a party asked the tribunal under s 33 to correct or interpret the award, or to make an additional award
      `the date the tribunal disposed of the s 33 request` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the tribunal disposed of that request
      `the date I appeal` IS A DATE @desc The day you appeal, or will appeal, to the Court
      `the Court is satisfied it will substantially affect a party's rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied that deciding the question will substantially affect the rights of a party
      `the Court is satisfied the tribunal was asked to decide it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied the tribunal was asked to decide the question
      `the Court is satisfied the decision is obviously wrong` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied, on the award's findings of fact, that the tribunal's decision is obviously wrong
      `the Court is satisfied it is of general public importance and the decision open to serious doubt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied the question is of general public importance and the decision at least open to serious doubt
      `the Court is satisfied it is just and proper for the Court to decide it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied it is just and proper, despite the agreement to arbitrate, for the Court to decide the question
GIVETH AN `Appeal answer`
`Can I appeal against our award` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF `no award has been made` `the award and me` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the appeal` (`Can I appeal against my award` (`the appeal built from` `it is a question of law arising out of the award` `the parties agreed to an appeal before the appeal period ended` `the Court is satisfied it will substantially affect a party's rights` `the Court is satisfied the tribunal was asked to decide it` `the Court is satisfied the decision is obviously wrong` `the Court is satisfied it is of general public importance and the decision open to serious doubt` `the Court is satisfied it is just and proper for the Court to decide it` `the date I received the award` `a section 33 request was made` `the date the tribunal disposed of the s 33 request` `the date I appeal`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Will the Court enforce my award (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) ss 35, 36)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the award and me` IS A `The award and me` @desc Whether an award has been made in your arbitration and, if so, whether it is in your favour, against you, or partly each
      `I apply to the Court in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied in writing to the Court for enforcement
      `I supply the original award or a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you supply the original award or a copy of it
      `the other party proves a ground in section 36(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the party you enforce against proves incapacity or invalidity, lack of notice, excess of submission, irregular tribunal or procedure, or that the award is not binding, set aside or suspended
      `the Court finds the dispute not arbitrable or enforcement against public policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Court's own finding under s 36(1)(b) (asked, not guessed)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Will the Court enforce our award for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF `there is no award in my favour to enforce` `the award and me` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Will the Court enforce my award` `I apply to the Court in writing` `I supply the original award or a copy` `the other party proves a ground in section 36(1)(a)` `the Court finds the dispute not arbitrable or enforcement against public policy`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I resist enforcement of the award against me (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 36(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the award and me` IS A `The award and me` @desc Whether an award has been made in your arbitration and, if so, whether it is in your favour, against you, or partly each
      `I prove a ground in section 36(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can prove one of the grounds in s 36(1)(a)(i)-(v)
      `the Court finds the dispute not arbitrable or enforcement against public policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Court's own finding under s 36(1)(b) (asked, not guessed)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I resist enforcement of our award` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a party to an arbitration agreement or an arbitration` THEN
        IF `there is no award against me to resist` `the award and me` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I resist enforcement of the award` `I prove a ground in section 36(1)(a)` `the Court finds the dispute not arbitrable or enforcement against public policy`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the arbitrator, or the person asked to be one (ss 12, 18, 24, 27D, 30, 31, 33)`

-- The questions here arise for every arbitrator, except the settlement (s 30(1)), the correction (s 33(2)) and, shared
-- with the party above, the arbitration after mediating (s 27D(4)-(6)).

@export Must I disclose circumstances that could raise doubts about my impartiality or independence (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 12(1), (2), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `there are circumstances likely to show a real danger of bias` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there are circumstances likely to give rise to justifiable doubts about your impartiality or independence: a real danger of bias in conducting the arbitration
      `I have been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already been appointed arbitrator (not only approached)
      `I have already told the parties of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you have been appointed, whether you have already told the parties of those circumstances
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I disclose what may show bias` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an arbitrator, or have been asked to be one` THEN `yes if` (`s 12(1), (2) -- the arbitrator must disclose the circumstances` `there are circumstances likely to show a real danger of bias` `I have been appointed` `I have already told the parties of them`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 18: "The parties must be treated with equality and each party must be given a reasonable opportunity of presenting
-- the party's case." Fixed for the role.
@export Must I treat the parties equally, and give each a reasonable opportunity to present its case (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 18)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I treat the parties equally` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an arbitrator, or have been asked to be one` THEN yes
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 24(2), from the arbitrator's seat: the baseline's rule, on a party's request.
@export Must I hold an oral hearing because a party asked for one (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 24(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a party asked me for an oral hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a party asked you for an oral hearing
      `the parties agreed that no hearings would be held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties agreed there would be no hearings
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I hold the oral hearing a party asked for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an arbitrator, or have been asked to be one` THEN `yes if` (`Must the tribunal hold an oral hearing` `a party asked me for an oral hearing` `the parties agreed that no hearings would be held`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 24(3)-(5): notice of hearings and inspections; what one party supplies "must be communicated to the other party";
-- "any expert report or evidentiary document on which the arbitral tribunal may rely ... must be communicated to the
-- parties." Fixed for the role.
@export Must I give the parties notice of hearings, and pass on to each what the other gives me and the expert reports I may rely on (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 24(3)-(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I pass on what the parties give me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an arbitrator, or have been asked to be one` THEN yes
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I act as mediator in the parties' dispute (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 27D(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the arbitration agreement provides for me to mediate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arbitration agreement provides for you, the arbitrator, to act as mediator
      `each party has consented in writing to my mediating` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every party has consented in writing to your acting as mediator
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I mediate the parties' dispute` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an arbitrator, or have been asked to be one` THEN `yes if` (`May our arbitrator act as mediator` `the arbitration agreement provides for me to mediate` `each party has consented in writing to my mediating`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What must I do now that the parties have settled during the arbitration (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 30(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the parties have settled during the arbitral proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties settled the dispute while the arbitration was under way
      `the parties asked me to record it as an award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties asked you to record the settlement as an award on agreed terms
      `I object to recording it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you object to recording it
GIVETH A `What I must do on a settlement`
`What must I do on the parties' settlement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an arbitrator, or have been asked to be one` THEN
        IF NOT `the parties have settled during the arbitral proceedings` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `s 30(1) -- what the tribunal must do on a settlement` `the parties asked me to record it as an award` `I object to recording it`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my award state its reasons (as arbitrator) (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 31(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the parties agreed no reasons would be given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties agreed that no reasons are to be given
      `it is an award on agreed terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the award records a settlement under s 30
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the award I make state its reasons` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an arbitrator, or have been asked to be one` THEN `yes if` (`Must my award state its reasons` `the parties agreed no reasons would be given` `it is an award on agreed terms`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many days of a party's request must I make a correction or interpretation I consider justified (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 33(2); the tribunal may extend the time, s 33(7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a party has asked me to correct or interpret the award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a party has asked you under s 33(1) to correct an error in the award or to interpret it
      `I consider the request justified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you consider the request justified
GIVETH A `Correction time`
`Within how many days must I make the correction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an arbitrator, or have been asked to be one` THEN
        IF NOT `a party has asked me to correct or interpret the award` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE IF `I consider the request justified` THEN within `s 33(2) -- the days the tribunal has to correct the award` ELSE `you need not make it, as you do not consider the request justified`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
